{"_id":"codex:protocol:08:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"protocol","title":"Protocol of Empathy & Temporal Reflection","seq":308,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","protocol","empathy"],"notes":"Perspective-taking and irreversibility checks prior to actuation."}
{"_id":"codex:protocol:08:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"policy","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"protocol","title":"Protocol of Empathy & Temporal Reflection","seq":308,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Before action: 1) Simulate consequences across affected agents (Empathy Engine). 2) Compute Temporal Irreversibility Index (TII). 3) If TII>threshold, escalate to tribunal/quorum. 4) Record perspective maps and mitigation plans. 5) Prefer reversible simulations first (A4)."}
